 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Has nucleotide phosphatase activity towards ATP, GTP,CTP, TTP and UTP. Hydrolyzes nucleoside diphosphates with lowerefficiency. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17291528}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=a ribonucleoside 5&apos;-triphosphate + H2O = a ribonucleoside5&apos;-diphosphate + H(+) + phosphate; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:23680,ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:43474,ChEBI:CHEBI:57930, ChEBI:CHEBI:61557; EC=3.6.1.15;BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=5 uM for ATP {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17291528};KM=46 uM for ADP {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17291528};KM=4 uM for GTP {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17291528};KM=6 uM for CTP {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17291528};KM=7 uM for TTP {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17291528};SUBUNIT: Monomer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17291528}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the THEP1 NTPase family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
