 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">NFS1_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">NFS1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.8.1.7</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">NIFS</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q9Y697-2_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_9054</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference75440</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_9054</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q9Y697_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the removal of elemental sulfur from cysteineto produce alanine. It supplies the inorganic sulfur for iron-sulfur (Fe-S) clusters. May be involved in the biosynthesis ofmolybdenum cofactor. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18650437}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=[sulfur carrier]-H + L-cysteine = [sulfur carrier]-SH +L-alanine; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:43892, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14737,Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14739, ChEBI:CHEBI:29917, ChEBI:CHEBI:35235,ChEBI:CHEBI:57972, ChEBI:CHEBI:64428; EC=2.8.1.7;COFACTOR:Name=pyridoxal 5&apos;-phosphate; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:597326;Evidence={ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O29689};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=434.75 uM for L-cysteine {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18650437};Note=Kinetic parameter was determined for the protein lackingthe 55 N-terminal amino acids and in a complex with LYRM4.;SUBUNIT: Binds ISCU/NIFUN (PubMed:11060020). Forms a complex withLYRM4 (PubMed:18650437, PubMed:19454487). Interacts with HSPA9(PubMed:26702583). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11060020,ECO:0000269|PubMed:18650437, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19454487,ECO:0000269|PubMed:26702583}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform Mitochondrial: Mitochondrion{ECO:0000269|PubMed:19454487, ECO:0000269|PubMed:26702583,ECO:0000269|PubMed:9885568}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform Cytoplasmic: Cytoplasm{ECO:0000269|PubMed:9885568}. Nucleus{ECO:0000269|PubMed:19454487, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9885568}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing, Alternative initiation; Named isoforms=3;Comment=Individual cells may vary AUG utilization in accordancewith changes in metabolic status, the cytosolic pH being astrong determinant of this modulation.;Name=Mitochondrial;IsoId=Q9Y697-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=Cytoplasmic;IsoId=Q9Y697-2; Sequence=VSP_018646;Name=3;IsoId=Q9Y697-3; Sequence=VSP_045860;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Predominantly expressed in heart and skeletalmuscle. Also found in brain, liver and pancreas.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the class-V pyridoxal-phosphate-dependentaminotransferase family. NifS/IscS subfamily. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">NFS1_HUMAN Reviewed; 457 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot.isoform/Q9Y697-2</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q53FP3</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot.isoform/Q9Y697-1</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

